{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>To the Jews there was light.</b> Its meaning is brightness, like the sense of אורה — like a person sitting in darkness who goes out into the air of the world, which is the opposite of without intermediary; so was the matter of Israel."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The phrase בלא אמצעי is textually difficult; read hyper-literally as 'without intermediary' though the construction is elliptical and possibly corrupt. The closing דבר ישר[אל] is resolved as 'the matter of Israel' based on standard Ibn Ezra usage."}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:18.623994721Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}